{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":19,"code":"PSA","name":"Psalms","testament":"OT"},"chapter":131,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"d","content":["A Song of degrees of David. "]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"PSA 131:1"},"LORD, my heart is not haughty, nor mine eyes lofty: neither do I exercise myself in great matters, or in things too high for me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 131:1"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"PSA 131:2"},"Surely I have behaved and quieted myself, as a child that is weaned of his mother: my soul ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," even as a weaned child. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 131:2"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"PSA 131:3"},"Let Israel hope in the LORD from henceforth and for ever. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 131:3"}]}]}
